      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "HILLDALE HILTON (9) has been hard to fault of late and he made it two in a row when successful at his latest appearance over 1609m at Menangle, getting home by 7 metres. Kept ticking over with subsequent trials, winning the most recent. She's done plenty of winning and the 30m is well deserved against lesser rivals. MANE ATTRACTION (2) is yet to win but has launched her career in promising fashion with four placings from six appearances. Recorded yet another strong performance last start when she battled on bravely to finish second over 2138m at this track, adding to her reputation as a genuine performer and the danger to the likely fave. DIZZYS HOPE (6) broke badly and finished a distant last over 2138m at this track when making her first appearance. Note she was in the market there and if she can get it right she can measure up. BOSTON BLIZZARD (1) has been about the mark of late and must be respected. Sound fourth at this track over 2138m last time.",
